{"postPage":{"id":"50f4b59b-6f60-4cbf-a243-aa9c0ba0b17f","post":{"id":"50f4b59b-6f60-4cbf-a243-aa9c0ba0b17f","title":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles","excerpt":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles My husband loves this dish! I'm sure I should make it more often than I do. The crunchy...","firstPublishedDate":"2017-11-17T14:35:00.000Z","lastPublishedDate":"2021-02-16T19:54:42.857Z","url":{"base":"https://www.theglasspantry.com","path":"/single-post/2017/11/05/chicken-chili-and-sourdough-cornbread-waffles"},"slug":"2017/11/05/chicken-chili-and-sourdough-cornbread-waffles","featured":false,"pinned":false,"categoryIds":["f3d78c3c-f7fd-498a-8718-f4c2bee77fea","6ba8db7a-6fe2-4b5a-83bf-acd0b1cbda4c","15abe877-7a05-4ea7-9f92-bfe7c73120b4","173f5020-85a4-4dfd-9e92-e3ed6303db2b","e444dbd4-a3f2-41ca-b0ae-85bd13111cd6","83230ff1-c2c7-4ffe-ad7b-bd212250ff1b"],"memberId":"2d3dcba5-39de-4c33-b11a-89d9248a0e51","hashtags":[],"commentingEnabled":true,"postCountInfo":{"comments":0,"likes":0,"views":398},"minutesToRead":5,"tagIds":["9d75596e-941f-4e4b-b109-5598983ec3b1","8e0f5a23-2d9b-470a-b32c-c4de612c8361","b0ee0525-46b5-40d5-a312-5418bfcef2f7","319b754a-7775-43b5-ae38-331bad2f7e9b","c4c99960-66c7-4033-b462-e1b7f254dc75","620215b0-a4f7-4c12-88dd-b8f67e755dcf","6598f707-1789-4257-b5a3-3e0b3875ef1d","e8198fcd-2969-4664-82d4-e3bd7316e011"],"relatedPostIds":[],"pricingPlanIds":[],"language":"en","metrics":{"comments":0,"likes":0,"views":398,"totalRatings":0,"averageRating":0},"seoData":{"tags":[{"type":"title","children":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles","custom":false,"disabled":false},{"type":"meta","props":{"name":"description","content":"Chicken Chili | Game Day Chicken Chili and Waffles | Chicken and Waffles | Sourdough Cornbread Waffles | Chili and Waffles"},"children":"","custom":false,"disabled":false}]},"richContent":{"nodes":[{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bel4j","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dlqi5","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"HEADING","id":"d87kf","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles","decorations":[]}}],"headingData":{"level":2,"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"avl4n","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cakri","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"65t9p","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_69223a813a62436f8615bb8e44924f69~mv2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles","caption":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3igg9","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"My husband loves this dish! I'm sure I should make it more often than I do. The crunchy sweet sourdough cornbread waffles make a great base for some spicy chicken chili. I like a little cheese and green onion on mine. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"693ai","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7rl60","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cff4h","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fbksv","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Pass around some sour cream and extra hot sauce too! I keep thinking there are a million slight variations that would make this recipe unique every time I make it so it really should be on the regular rotation for the winter. I'm thinking some chopped green chilies or pickled jalapenos added to the waffle batter or a hand full of shredded cheese would make sense here. Maybe a green chicken chili next time?","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"2893l","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"1mmbv","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_724f0f74aa3e4080aa98271c482427ad~mv2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Chicken Chili and Sourdough Cornbread Waffles"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5hnlk","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fv92c","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I call these cornbread waffles because I really do use my cornbread recipe to make them. I use a polenta grind instead of traditional cornmeal because I like the added crunch it has. When I make cornbread I use a lot of honey in place of white sugar because I like the tangy flavor of the honey and the sticky moisture it brings to a nice pan of cornbread but I really didn't want that in this recipe so I used regular white sugar. It makes a much more crisp sweet waffle.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9rtg3","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4on5d","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cnr0o","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Before I start making the waffles I need to get the chili started. I chopped up some nice boneless chicken breasts and started browning them lightly in 1 tablespoon of olive oil in my dutch oven.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"agiti","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Man this thing really gets a work out at my house! Yes, This is the same dutch oven I use for a lot of my bread baking too.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"biuv0","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"2oru","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_571fc60044164c51b11db132a02c31d7~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Starting the Chicken Chili"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"6h0h1","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dftqf","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I brown them on a medium high heat just until they start to become opaque and then I start adding the the rest of the ingredients in the chili starting with the vegetables.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"55teo","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"brg1h","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"1098d","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_5eaa282b21fb437b872648d6783c4f7b~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Chicken Chili ingredients"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"eqlec","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9gekc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Today I'm using 3 small poblano chilies from my late summer garden harvest. They are tiny and starting to turn red. They're a little sweet and mild to medium hot. I'm also using 3 jalapenos from my garden and these puppies are really hot. I've never had hot jalapenos from my garden until this year but wow! These are really good. I recently received some great looking ghost chilies from a friend who grows them. Next chili, I'm using one of those!","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"6u2fa","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"487q8","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"But for today, I also have a green bell pepper, half a red onion, some celery and a small head of garlic from the garden.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"bod38","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"5r7g7","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_6a3e07db1b3f409ca82b86ea50629d4b~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Chicken Chili"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cjqak","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}},{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"After chopping up the veggies and adding them to the chicken in the dutch oven.","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"7sur7","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c3vuc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"4l215","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5l2du","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"eg923","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_0212fafd124b4debb904010ce43630e0~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Chicken Chili Seasonings"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"8raqa","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5sk7m","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"These are the spices that go into this chili. Smoked Spanish Paprika, Cayenne Pepper,  hot Smoked Hatch Chili Powder from New Mexico and a mild Ancho chili powder, think chocolate-like. I also used some Cumin that's not pictured here.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"8pjta","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"aqh0g","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"168mv","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"evngc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I like to make my own spice blends and season dishes using individual spices because I always feel like I just don't know about the stabilizers and desiccants and color enhancers that are added to most spice blends. Plus, the actual spices may not be listed on the package and I know I can't stomach too much oregano personally. So this is one way for me to clean up my eating. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"56a5p","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"e86mg","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_dbaeebb2ca2244638c050184fbe0d216~mv2_d_4032_3024_s_4_2.jpg"},"width":4032,"height":3024},"altText":"Adding my spices to the chili"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fmd6k","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Adding Spices to the Chicken Chili ","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"dch6l","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"6upvc","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"fn26s","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"5fedl","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I let the vegetables saute until they are slightly translucent and then add in the chopped garlic and the spices. I stir them for a few minutes to gently toast them and bring out the flavors before adding in the wet ingredients.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"63g9t","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c4mpn","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"IMAGE","id":"ddh7o","nodes":[],"imageData":{"containerData":{"width":{"size":"CONTENT"},"alignment":"CENTER","textWrap":true},"image":{"src":{"id":"577c92_e4ac26fb1349462f86c27add89f03231~mv2_d_3536_2366_s_2.jpg"},"width":3536,"height":2366},"altText":"Spicy Chicken Chili","caption":"The Original Spicy Chicken Chili"}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"cbo4m","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Spicy Chicken Chili Simmering ","decorations":[{"type":"BOLD","fontWeightValue":700},{"type":"ITALIC","italicData":true}]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"ej623","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"CENTER"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"22vt8","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"After adding the wet ingredients, 2 cans of beans half drained, 1 can of tomatoes and 1 can of tomato soup,  give it a good stir and turn the heat down so the pot of chili can simmer while the crispy waffles are being made. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"35n0v","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"3bnf4","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"I know some of you will be thinking, \"OMG! Campbell's Tomato Soup?!\" But I tell you, sometimes you need just one can of Campbell's soup. It makes a crazy difference in the chili. When I don't use it, I definitely need to simmer for a much longer time to get the creaminess I'm looking for in the chili. It's something about the tomatoes breaking down over a long slow simmer that I sometimes just don't have time for. ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c2svi","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"c0e2d","nodes":[],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"f348n","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":"Recently I updated several pictures for this post because the original ones were quite dark and I have a great new camera on my Galaxy Note! The new pictures feature a slightly different homemade chili that's basically the same but with some butter beans instead of kidney beans, shredded cooked turkey (leftovers :0) instead of chicken, and some slightly different garnishes. I always use that can of tomato soup and spice it up similarly. It just depends on what I have on hand, Feel free to experiment with your own spice cupboard and get creative if you don't have exactly what I've used here.","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"1h0q6","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"f2ka3","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"6o49v","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"PARAGRAPH","id":"9k7lq","nodes":[{"type":"TEXT","id":"","nodes":[],"textData":{"text":" ","decorations":[]}}],"paragraphData":{"textStyle":{"textAlignment":"AUTO"},"indentation":0}},{"type":"GAL